          "type": "text",
          "title": "Demand driver",
          "text": "In Q1 FY2027, management reported AI orders of $24.4 billion and said it raised its FY2027 AI server revenue expectation to $60 billion. These are prior-quarter reported indicators, not Q2 results.",
          "status": "reported",
          "evidence": {
            "source_id": "dell_results_1",
            "quote": "We’re increasing our AI server revenue expectations for FY27 to $60 billion"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "Credit and financing risk",
          "text": "Financing receivable allowances reflect expected credit losses, and Dell monitors broader economic indicators for their possible impact on future credit loss performance.",
          "status": "reported",
          "evidence": {
            "source_id": "sec_dell_10q",
            "quote": "The Company continues to monitor broader economic indicators and their potential impact on future credit loss performance."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "Funding-structure contingency",
          "text": "If specified receivable-performance criteria are not met and the facility cannot be restructured, further receivable funding may stop and expected cash flows from over-collateralization may be delayed.",
